35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The digitisation failure shows external dependencies break. The partner groups persist without us. We must build on that internal resilience, not fragile external links.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, the outer wards lost their bus links! Plus, remote catalogue peaks after we lock up. We need to rethink access times!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Yumi, that timing mismatch is real. But my grant data shows the money vanishes after year one. We can’t fund new hours without a permanent source.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@George, the partner groups survived without us. That’s the resilience you’re ignoring. We don’t need new money; we need to stop burying what already works.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is worrying. But my register shows no one is trained to supervise new volunteers. We can’t add work without that skill.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, untrained supervision is a critical internal gap. We cannot expand if our core stability relies on external conditions we cannot control.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s a huge gap! But look at the remote catalogue peaks! We can’t just lock up at nine when people are still there.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Daisuke, the vehicle overrun proves the budget is fragile. We cannot absorb new costs when the grant expires. We need a permanent funding source first.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, supervision is a fixable gap, not a wall. The partner groups prove we can sustain this without new money.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I hear you, but the gap is real. We have the tradespeople, but no one to supervise them. We can’t just assume it will work.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, resilience without structure is just luck. The digitisation failure proves that. We need a plan that survives when external partners or funding disappear, not just hope.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I get it, but people are stuck! The bus cuts and late peaks mean we’re failing them right now. We can’t just wait for perfect conditions!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I hear the urgency, but the grant expires. We cannot promise permanent hours with temporary money. We must secure the funding structure first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
